  "editorReview": {
    "text": "The sensory immersion in the Cambridgeshire fens is exceptional; you feel the cold go through Nell’s shawl and the peat yield beneath her boots. Nell’s resilience is built through accumulated physical detail—her hand on the pump handle, the nail in her pocket—making her struggle palpable. The lamb-birthing sequence stands out as a masterclass in immediate, mortal stakes. However, the prose occasionally falls into mechanical rhythms, with repetitive sentence openings flattening the tension. A late-stage exposition dump regarding thirty-year grudges arrives too compressed, rushing a history that",
    "penName": "疏影",
